<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>
  This project investigated the dynamic analysis of serial-parallel
  Gough–Stewart manipulators, including hybrid, redundant, and
  hyper-redundant configurations.
</p>

<h2>Contributions</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Developed inverse-dynamics models using virtual-work and Jacobian-based formulations.</li>
  <li>Implemented inverse kinematics and trajectory-tracking simulations.</li>
  <li>Performed actuator-force validation.</li>
  <li>Modeled serial-parallel systems in MATLAB and Simscape.</li>
  <li>Investigated minimal and base inertial parameters.</li>
</ul>

